{"id":"c21bafd4e0cb5f89","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-df-zfc-pcf2-pseudo-power.md","title":"ZFC Pcf2 Pseudo Power","display":"df-zfc-pcf2-pseudo-power — ZFC Pcf2 Pseudo Power","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-pcf2-pseudo-power","aliases":["58-df-zfc-pcf2-pseudo-power"],"display":"df-zfc-pcf2-pseudo-power — ZFC Pcf2 Pseudo Power","depends_on":["[[58-df-zfc-pcf2-possible-cofinality]]","[[58-df-cardinal]]","[[58-df-cofinality]]","[[58-df-equinumerous]]","[[58-df-zfc-hartogs-number]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-pcf2-pseudo-power"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-pcf2-pseudo-power</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-pcf2-pseudo-power — ZFC Pcf2 Pseudo Power"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"13b44f8137f7b9f8\" href=\"?note=13b44f8137f7b9f8\" title=\"58-df-zfc-pcf2-possible-cofinality\">58-df-zfc-pcf2-possible-cofinality</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"315ad00b8744fdfc\" href=\"?note=315ad00b8744fdfc\" title=\"58-df-cofinality\">58-df-cofinality</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"28c79fde9f892bfe\" href=\"?note=28c79fde9f892bfe\" title=\"58-df-equinumerous\">58-df-equinumerous</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"4dad079dff660754\" href=\"?note=4dad079dff660754\" title=\"58-df-zfc-hartogs-number\">58-df-zfc-hartogs-number</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span> (singular cardinal candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span> (pseudo-power value)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta\">\\(\\theta\\)</span> (possible-cofinality value)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\in\\mathcal P(\\mu)\">\\(A\\in\\mathcal P(\\mu)\\)</span> (progressive cofinal set of regular cardinals of size <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{cf}(\\mu)\">\\(\\operatorname{cf}(\\mu)\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"h\">\\(h\\)</span> (uniform Hartogs bound)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{cf},\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S,\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{cf},\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S,\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S\\)</span> (sourced operator and predicates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HartogsNumber}_S,\\mathrm{ZfcPcf2PossibleCofinality}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{HartogsNumber}_S,\\mathrm{ZfcPcf2PossibleCofinality}_S\\)</span> (sourced predicates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcPcf2PseudoPower}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcPcf2PseudoPower}_S\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}pcf2\\text{-}pseudo\\text{-}power}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcPcf2PseudoPower}_S(\\mu,\\lambda)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\mu)\\land\\operatorname{cf}(\\mu)&lt;\\mu\\land\n\\exists h\\in V\\;\\Bigl[\n\\mathrm{HartogsNumber}_S\\bigl(h,\\mathcal P(\\mu\\times\\mu)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\lambda=\\sup\\Bigl\\{\\theta\\in h:\\exists A\\in\\mathcal P(\\mu)\\;\\bigl(\n\\sup A=\\mu\n\\land\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(A,\\operatorname{cf}(\\mu))\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{48mm}\\land\\mathrm{ZfcPcf2PossibleCofinality}_S(A,\\theta)\n\\bigr)\\Bigr\\}\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}pcf2\\text{-}pseudo\\text{-}power}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcPcf2PseudoPower}_S(\\mu,\\lambda)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\mu)\\land\\operatorname{cf}(\\mu)&lt;\\mu\\land\n\\exists h\\in V\\;\\Bigl[\n\\mathrm{HartogsNumber}_S\\bigl(h,\\mathcal P(\\mu\\times\\mu)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\lambda=\\sup\\Bigl\\{\\theta\\in h:\\exists A\\in\\mathcal P(\\mu)\\;\\bigl(\n\\sup A=\\mu\n\\land\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(A,\\operatorname{cf}(\\mu))\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{48mm}\\land\\mathrm{ZfcPcf2PossibleCofinality}_S(A,\\theta)\n\\bigr)\\Bigr\\}\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The canonical possible-cofinality predicate already quantifies the appropriate ultrafilter quotients and enforces progressiveness.  The additional clauses make <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> cofinal in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span> and equinumerous with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{cf}(\\mu)\">\\(\\operatorname{cf}(\\mu)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Every product over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\subseteq\\mu\">\\(A\\subseteq\\mu\\)</span> is coded inside <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P(\\mu\\times\\mu)\">\\(\\mathcal P(\\mu\\times\\mu)\\)</span>, so its possible cofinalities lie below the displayed uniform Hartogs bound; the supremum is therefore formed from a bounded set.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-zfc-pcf2-possible-cofinality","status":"resolved","id":"13b44f8137f7b9f8","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-pcf2-possible-cofinality]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ca